===Etymology===
Alteration ({{m|de||-ch}} due to {{m|de|Lurch}}) of {{der|de|gmh|mol}}, {{m|gmh|molle}}, from {{der|de|goh|mol}}, {{m|goh|mollo|mol(l)o}}, from {{der|de|gem-pro|*mulô}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*molh₂-o-}} (compare {{cog|lt|mulvas|mul̃vas|t=yellow, clayey}}, {{cog|la|mulleus|t=ruddy (shoes)}}, {{cog|sa|मल|tr=mála|t=dirt}}), from {{m|ine-pro|*melh₂-|t=dark color}}.<ref>Wolfgang Pfeifer, ed., ''Etymologisches Wörterbuch des Deutschen'', s.v. “Molch” (Munich: Deutscher Taschenbucher Vertrag, 2005).</ref> More at {{l|de|malen}}.

